Article 7 (Applicability to Collection of Reduced Acquisition Tax as Penalty)
The amended provisions of Article 178 (2) shall begin to apply from the first cases where acquisition tax is reduced on real estate after this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Special Cases concerning Reduction or Exemption for Previous Agricultural Corporations)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of provisions, with exemption of the subparagraphs, of Article 11 (1), acquisition tax shall be exempted on farmland acquired by an agricultural corporation whose registration for incorporation is made before January 1, 2020 within two years from the date of registration for incorporation to use for farming, woodland acquired to create farmland pursuant to relevant statutes and facilities falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 6 (2). In such cases, Article 11 (3) shall apply to collecting the reduced portion of acquisition tax as a penalty.
