(1) The amended provisions of Article 31 (1) and (4) shall begin to apply from the first tax liability arising after this Act enters into force: Provided, That the part concerning the Local Tax Act within the amended provisions of Article 31 (4) shall begin to apply from the first case where a rental business entity acquires multi-family housing and officetels for rent and registers them after this Act enters into force or a rental business entity newly registers multi-family housing and officetels held before this Act enters into force.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 31 (5), the former provisions shall apply to collecting the property tax reduced or exempted before this Act enters into force, as a penalty.
(3) The amended provisions of Article 31 (7) shall begin to apply from the first case where the Korea Land and Housing Corporation newly builds and supplies houses or buildings by changing or demolishing the number of units or structures, etc. after purchasing them pursuant to Article 43 (1) of the Special Act on Public Housing after this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to Reduction or Exemption for Long-Term Private Rental Housing)
(1) The amended provisions of Article 31-3 (1) shall begin to apply from the first tax liability arising after this Act enters into force: Provided, That the part concerning Article 4 of the Local Tax Act within the amended provisions of Article 31-3 (1) shall begin to apply from the first case where a person who intends to rent publicly-funded private rental housing defined in subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Private Rental Housing and long-term private rental housing defined in subparagraph 5 of that Article acquires multi-family housing and officetels for rent and registers them after this Act enters into force or newly registers multi-family housing and officetels held before this Act enters into forced.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 31-3 (2), the former provisions shall apply to collecting the property tax reduced or exempted before this Act enters into force as a penalty.
Article 6 (Applicability to Reduction or Exemption for Persons Concluded Agreements to Sell Houses for Rental Purposes of Public Housing Project Operators)
The amended provisions of Article 31-5 (1) and (2) shall begin to apply from the first case where an agreement is concluded to sell houses, etc. to a public housing project operator after this Act enters into force.
Article 7 (Applicability to Reduction or Exemption for Houses subject to Reverse Annuity Mortgage)
The amended provisions of Article 35 (1) 2 (a) and (b) shall begin to apply from the first case where with respect to registration of a house provided as a security, which meets the criteria for providing guarantees for reverse annuity mortgages, a person who provides the house as a security assumes registration license tax after this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Applicability to Reduction or Exemption for Real Estate to Be Used for Research Institutes Affiliated with Middle-Standing Enterprises)
The amended provisions of Article 46 (3) shall begin to apply from the first case where a middle-standing enterprise falling under Article 10 (1) 1 (a) (ii) of the Act on Restriction of Special Cases concerning Taxation acquires real estate to use directly for a research institute affiliated with the enterprise after this Act enters into force.
Article 9 (Applicability to Reduction or Exemption for Buildings with Seismic Performance)
The amended provisions of the main clause of Article 47-4 (3) shall also apply to the buildings that were certified as an earthquake-safe facility less than 180 days ago.
Article 10 (Applicability to Reduction or Exemption for Re-Acquisition of Assets by Small or Medium Enterprises)
The amended provisions of Article 57-3 (4) shall also apply to small or medium enterprises that sell assets to the Korea Asset Management Corporation pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 11 (Applicability to Tax Credit for Electronic Filing of Individual Local Income Tax)
The Amended provisions of Article 167-3 (1) shall begin to apply from the first case where individual local income tax is reported through electronic filing under Article 25 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes after this Act enters into force.
Article 12 (Transitional Measures concerning Collection of Reduction or Exemption of Acquisition Tax as Penalty on First-Time Home Buyers)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 36-3 (4) 1 through 3, the former provisions shall apply to collecting the acquisition tax reduced or exempted before this Act enters into force as a penalty.
Article 13 (Transitional Measures concerning Reduction or Exemption of Property Registered after acquisition due to Merger between Financial Companies)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of the main clause of Article 57-2 (10), the former provisions shall apply to the reduction of registration license tax on property registered within three years from the date of merger when the merger between financial companies is made before this Act enters into force.
Article 14 (Transitional Measures concerning Imposition of Acquisition Tax on Replacement Motor Vehicles)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of the proviso of Article 66 (1), the former provisions shall apply to the imposition of acquisition tax on the excess where the value of motor vehicles, etc. acquired through exchange before this Act enters into force exceeds the value of the previous motor vehicles, etc.
Article 15 (Transitional Measures concerning Reduction or Exemption for Relocating Corporations and Factories to Provinces)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 79 (1), where a corporation directly engaging in business by establishing its head office or main office in a large city before this Act enters into force relocates its head office or main office to an area other than over-concentration limitation zones, the former provisions shall apply to the reduction, exemption, and collection as a penalty on acquisition tax and property tax.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 79 (2), the former provisions shall apply to the exemption of registration license tax where the corporation registered in a large city before this Act enters into force relocates its head office or main office in an area other than over-concentration limitation zones.
(3) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 80 (1), the former provisions shall apply to the reduction, exemption, and collection as a penalty on acquisition tax and property tax where a person directly engaging in business with factory facilities equipped with in a large city before this Act enters into force closes such factory and relocates its factory to an area other than over-concentration limitation zones, where the establishment of a factory is not prohibited or restricted.
Article 16 (Transitional Measures concerning Tax Credit for Payment through Automatic Transfer)
The former provisions shall apply to tax credit for taxpayers who files for payment of local taxes by electronic services and automatic transfer before municipal ordinance is promulgated or amended pursuant to the amended provision of Article 92-2 (1) 1 and 2.

